# GL.module's absolute references into its data, reviewed (tools/baserel_check.py).
# They reach the data as loaded, which no program's copy is. One regular
# expression a line, for the check's report line; "write:" lines allow
# writes. Reviewed 8 October 2026, Mesa 26.2.4.
#
# glsl's builtin_types.cpp: the gl_*_fields tables (the fields of GLSL's
# built-in uniform structs) are "static const", so GCC reaches them by their
# absolute address everywhere, but glsl_struct_field has a constructor, so
# they are filled in by the file's static constructor, which runs in every
# program's open. The values are the same each time (text addresses of the
# names, built-in glsl_types in the code, small numbers), so every program
# reads one shared table that each start writes again with the same values,
# and it lives as long as the module is loaded.
write: ^write of \.bss\._ZL\d+gl_\w+_fields\+0x[0-9a-f]+ of libglsl\.a\(builtin_types\.cpp\.o\), from the code at .*\(\.text\S* of libglsl\.a\(builtin_types\.cpp\.o\)\)$
^address of \.bss\._ZL\d+gl_\w+_fields\+0x[0-9a-f]+ of libglsl\.a\(builtin_types\.cpp\.o\), from the code at .*\(\.text\S* of libglsl\.a\(builtin_types\.cpp\.o\)\)$
# glsl's ir_print_visitor.cpp: visit(ir_variable)'s static const tables of
# names (mode, interpolation, precision), only read.
^address of \.data\+0x0 of libglsl\.a\(ir_print_visitor\.cpp\.o\), from the code at __ZN16ir_print_visitor5visitEP11ir_variable\+
# nir_opt_undef.c: the shader_blake3s[] local array's first values, copied
# onto the stack.
^address of \.data\+0x0 of libnir\.a\(nir_opt_undef\.c\.o\), from the code at _nir_opt_undef\+
